# Belt and braces (not load-bearing on their own — see the note below).
#
# The architectural answer to "what stops a URL reaching PHP source or
# secrets" is that there is nothing sensitive under public_html/ at all: no
# config.php, no store.php, no site.json, no admin.json, no session files —
# none of it exists anywhere under the web root, in any form, at any path.
# See docs/php-admin-architecture.md section 8.2. These two rules are a
# cheap second layer on top of that, not a substitute for it: even if a
# future developer drops a stray second .php file into this directory by
# mistake, it is denied by default, and only api.php itself is ever granted.

<FilesMatch "\.php$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
<Files "api.php">
    Require all granted
</Files>
